-- title:
--   Finiteness and separability over K(j(q^N))
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field, let $N$ be a nonzero natural number whose image $(N : K)$ in $K$ is nonzero, and let `data` be a datum of type `ModularPolynomialData N`, that is, a polynomial $\Phi \in \mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ which is monic (in $Y$), whose degree equals $\psi(N) = \sum_{d \mid N,\ d \text{ squarefree}} N/d$, and which satisfies $\Phi(j(q), j(q^N)) = 0$ as an identity of Laurent series over $\mathbb{Q}$, the evaluation being $X \mapsto j(q)$ and $Y \mapsto j(q^N)$. Write $j_K(q) \in K((q))$ for the Laurent series $q^{-1}$ times the image of the integral power series `jNum` under $\mathbb{Z} \to K$, and $j_K(q^N)$ for its image under the substitution $q \mapsto q^N$ (reindexing exponents by multiplication by $N$). Let $F_N = K(j_K(q), j_K(q^N))$ be the intermediate field of $K((q))$ over $K$ generated by these two series. Then $F_N$ is finite-dimensional over the intermediate field of $F_N$ generated over $K$ by $j_K(q^N)$ alone, and the extension $F_N$ over that subfield is separable.
--
--   This is the statement that the plane model of $X_0(N)$ given by the modular polynomial is a finite separable covering of the $j(q^N)$-line in characteristic not dividing $N$; it is the companion, with the two generators interchanged, of the corresponding assertion over $K(j(q))$. It supplies the finiteness and separability hypotheses needed when the lemma on simple points of the plane model is applied in the $j(q^N)$-orientation, for instance in the non-vanishing of $\partial \Phi_N/\partial X$ and in the identification of Frobenius on fibres.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_finiteDimensional_and_isSeparable_adjoin_jqNModC_of_natCast_ne_zero.lean

